{
  "$comment": [
    "The money census for the Node binding's output surface, maintained by hand.",
    "test/money-exactness.js reads it and asserts that",
    "(a) every field listed under `money` has a `<field>Exact` string twin in the",
    "generated index.d.ts, and",
    "(b) every f64 field on every `*Output` struct in src/lib.rs appears here as",
    "either money or notMoney.",
    "So a new float money field without a twin fails, and any new float output",
    "field fails until someone decides which it is.",
    "`notMoney` holds rates, percentages, scores, quantities, distances and",
    "durations: values that are not currency amounts and need no exact twin.",
    "`methodArgs` is the same census for bare f64 METHOD ARGUMENTS, which are",
    "not fields on any struct and so are invisible to the checks above."
  ],
  "twinSuffix": "Exact",
  "methodArgs": {
    "$comment": [
      "Money that arrives as a bare f64 argument rather than as a struct field.",
      "test/money-exactness.js parses every `#[napi]` fn signature in src/lib.rs,",
      "requires each f64 argument to be listed here, and fails when one listed",
      "under `money` has no `<arg>_exact: Option<String>` sibling argument in the",
      "same signature. Keys are `<owner>.<method>`: the owner is the enclosing",
      "inherent `impl` block (`(module)` for a free `#[napi] pub fn`), and the",
      "method is the name JavaScript calls \u2014 the attribute's `js_name` when it",
      "sets one, otherwise the camelCased Rust fn name.",
      "The sibling must be the LAST parameter of the signature, not merely",
      "present: that is what keeps callers written before the exact half existed",
      "working unchanged, and the test asserts the position."
    ],
    "money": {
      "Carts.setTax": [
        "taxAmount"
      ],
      "CostAccounting.updateAverageCost": [
        "unitCost"
      ],
      "Credit.adjustCreditLimit": [
        "newLimit"
      ],
